An object may serve as a dict key or set element only if it is hashable, and mutable built-ins deliberately are not. Consequently:

- coordinates are `tuple`, never `list`;
- a set of sets must be a set of `frozenset`;
- a custom class needs `__eq__` and `__hash__`, covered in **Python Classes**.

```python
lookup = {(r, c): value for r, row in enumerate(grid) for c, value in enumerate(row)}
distinct = {frozenset(s) for s in list_of_sets}
```
